{"sounds":{"intro":"Proto-Indo-European (PIE) is the reconstructed ancestor of English, Spanish, Russian, Hindi, Greek, Persian and hundreds more, spoken about 4500 to 3500 BC. Nobody wrote it down. Every form here is a scholarly reconstruction, marked with an asterisk (*). Treat it as the best guess of linguists, not as a real record. Forms differ between scholars, and the \"say\" line is only a rough convention.","rows":[["h₁ / h₂ / h₃","the three \"laryngeals\", unknown sounds like a breathy \"h\"; h₂ coloured a nearby \"e\" into \"a\", h₃ into \"o\"","*h₂ster-"],["ḱ / ǵ / ǵʰ","\"k\", \"g\" and breathy \"gh\" said further forward in the mouth","*ḱlew-"],["kʷ / gʷ / gʷʰ","\"kw\", \"gw\" and breathy \"gwh\"","*kʷetwóres"],["bʰ / dʰ","\"b\" and \"d\" with a puff of breath","*bʰréh₂tēr"],["ḱ vs k","in Latin the first became \"k\" and in Russian it became \"s\", which is why \"hundred\" is \"centum\" but \"sto\"","*ḱm̥tóm"]],"notes":["A mark over a vowel (ē, ō) means long. A small circle under r, l, m, n (r̥, l̥, m̥, n̥) means the consonant acted as a vowel. An accent (´) shows where the stress fell.","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. Everything is reconstructed and unreviewed. Many details are argued about among scholars."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","*h₁óynos","HOY-nos"],["two","*dwóh₁","DWOH"],["three","*tréyes","TRAY-es"],["four","*kʷetwóres","kwet-WOR-es"],["five","*pénkʷe","PEN-kweh"],["six","*swéḱs","SWEKS"],["seven","*septḿ̥","sep-TM"],["eight","*h₃eḱtṓ","okh-TOH"],["nine","*h₁néwn̥","NEH-wn"],["ten","*déḱm̥","DEK-m"],["hundred","*ḱm̥tóm","km-TOM"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"simple-words-and-sentences","title":"Simple words and sentences","items":[["yes / it is so","*h₁és-ti","ES-tee"],["no / not","*ne","neh"],["do not (command)","*méh₁","MEH"],["hail / be healthy","*h₂wén-ti","WEN-tee"],["give!","*déh₃-dʰi","DOH-dee"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"about-me","title":"About me","items":[["I","*h₁éǵ","eg"],["you (one person)","*túh₂","too"],["he / that","*só","so"],["we","*wéy","way"],["I am","*h₁és-mi","ES-mee"],["you are","*h₁és-si","ES-see"],["he is","*h₁és-ti","ES-tee"],["I know","*ǵéh₃-n-h₂-mi","GNOH-mee"],["I see","*wéyd-mi","WAYD-mee"],["I give","*dídoh₃-mi","DEE-doh-mee"],["what?","*kʷid","kwid"],["who?","*kʷis","kwis"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and family","items":[["father","*ph₂tḗr","pa-TAIR"],["mother","*méh₂tēr","MAH-tair"],["son","*suHnús","soo-NOOS"],["daughter","*dʰugh₂tḗr","doo-ga-TAIR"],["brother","*bʰréh₂tēr","BRAH-tair"],["sister","*swésōr","SWEH-sor"],["man","*h₂nḗr","a-NAIR"],["person","*dʰéǵʰōm","DEH-gom"],["king","*h₃rḗǵs","ROHGS"]]},{"id":"nature-and-animals","title":"Nature and animals","items":[["sun","*séh₂wōl","SAH-wol"],["moon","*méh₁n̥s","MAY-ns"],["star","*h₂stḗr","a-STAIR"],["sky / day god","*dyḗws","DYAYWS"],["night","*nókʷts","NOKWTS"],["water","*wódr̥","WOD-r"],["fire","*péh₂wr̥","PAH-wr"],["earth","*dʰéǵʰōm","DEH-gom"],["tree / oak","*dóru","DOH-roo"],["dog","*ḱwṓ","KWOH"],["horse","*h₁éḱwos","EH-kwos"],["cow","*gʷṓws","GWOWS"],["sheep","*h₃éwis","OH-wis"],["wolf","*wĺ̥kʷos","WL-kwos"]]},{"id":"body-and-home","title":"Body and home","items":[["foot","*pṓds","PODS"],["hand","*ǵʰésr̥","GES-r"],["eye","*h₃ókʷs","OKWS"],["heart","*ḱḗrd","KAIRD"],["name","*h₁néh₃mn̥","NOH-mn"],["house","*dómh₂s","DOM-s"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["new","*néwos","NEH-wos"],["old","*senos","SEH-nos"],["red","*h₁rewdʰ-","REW-dh"]]},{"id":"verbs-root","title":"Verbs (root)","items":[["to be","*h₁es-","es"],["to eat","*h₁ed-","ed"],["to drink","*péh₃-","POH"],["to go","*h₁ey-","ey"],["to carry","*bʰer-","ber"],["to know","*ǵneh₃-","GNOH"],["to hear","*ḱlew-","KLEW"],["to sit","*sed-","sed"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["PIE had no he/she/it as we know them. It used the pointing word *so (m), *seh₂ (f), *tod (n) meaning \"this or that\"."],"rows":[["I","*h₁éǵ","eg"],["you","*túh₂","too"],["he / that","*só","so"],["she / that (f)","*séh₂","SAH"],["we","*wéy","way"],["you (pl)","*yuHs","yoos"]],"ex":[["I am a king","*h₁éǵ h₁és-mi h₃rḗǵs","eg ES-mee ROHGS"],["you are a man","*túh₂ h₁és-si h₂nḗr","too ES-see a-NAIR"],["he is my father","*só h₁és-ti ph₂tḗr","so ES-tee pa-TAIR"]]},{"id":"verb-endings","title":"Verb endings","text":["PIE verbs took endings for the person: -mi (I), -si (you), -ti (he/she), -mes (we), -te (you pl.), -(e)nti (they). Spanish, Latin and Greek endings come from these."],"rows":[["I am","*h₁és-mi","ES-mee"],["you are","*h₁és-si","ES-see"],["he is","*h₁és-ti","ES-tee"],["we are","*h₁s-més","smes"],["you (pl) are","*h₁s-té","ste"],["they are","*h₁s-énti","SEN-tee"]],"ex":[["I eat","*h₁éd-mi","ED-mee"],["you give","*dídoh₃-si","DEE-doh-see"],["he carries","*bʰér-e-ti","BER-eh-tee"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put *ne before the verb: \"*ne h₁és-ti\" (he is not). For a command use *méh₁: \"*méh₁ h₁éd-e\" (do not eat)."],"rows":[["not","*ne","neh"],["do not (command)","*méh₁","MEH"]],"ex":[["he is","*h₁és-ti","ES-tee"],["he is not","*ne h₁és-ti","neh ES-tee"],["I know","*ǵéh₃-n-h₂-mi","GNOH-mee"],["I do not know","*ne ǵéh₃-n-h₂-mi","neh GNOH-mee"],["eat!","*h₁éd-e","ED-eh"],["do not eat!","*méh₁ h₁éd-e","MEH ED-eh"]]}],"name":"Proto-Indo-European","id":"ine","flag":"ine","note":""}